  "grammar.audit.practice.10.7.option.1": "Enter at 9:00 with outside food.",
  "grammar.audit.practice.10.7.option.2": "Wait until 18:00.",
  "grammar.audit.practice.10.8.question": "Find the error in this polite description.",
  "grammar.audit.practice.10.8.prompt": "The intended meaning is “The room was not quiet”.",
  "grammar.audit.practice.10.8.success": "The な adjective uses しずかではありませんでした (or しずかじゃなかったです), not くなかったです.",
  "grammar.audit.practice.10.8.error": "The な adjective uses しずかではありませんでした (or しずかじゃなかったです), not くなかったです.",
  "grammar.audit.practice.10.9.question": "Build a future intention.",
  "grammar.audit.practice.10.9.prompt": "“I intend to go to Japan”. Start with わたしは.",
  "grammar.audit.practice.10.9.success": "Intention uses the dictionary form: いくつもりです.",
  "grammar.audit.practice.10.9.error": "Intention uses the dictionary form: いくつもりです.",
  "grammar.audit.theory.02.11": "<span class=\"grammar-contrast\"><span>はは <b>は</b><small>topic: my mother</small></span><span>りょうり <b>が</b><small>skill: cooking</small></span><span>じょうずです<small>is skilled</small></span></span>は organizes who we talk about; が identifies the skill we describe. They are not interchangeable here.",
  "grammar.audit.theory.02.11.title": "Topic and skill",
  "grammar.audit.theory.03.13": "<span class=\"grammar-contrast\"><span>うち <b>で</b><small>place of an action</small></span><span>うち <b>に</b><small>destination or existence</small></span><span>うち <b>へ</b><small>direction of movement</small></span></span>うちでべんきょうします = I study at home. うちにいきます = I go home. うちへいきます = I go towards home.",
  "grammar.audit.theory.03.13.title": "Place, destination and direction",
  "grammar.audit.theory.04.9": "At a shop you ask for にまいのかみ (two sheets), みっつのりんご (three apples) and いっぽんのえんぴつ (a pencil). Choose the counter for what you count, not from an isolated list. まい: flat; ほん: long; つ: objects in general.",
  "grammar.audit.theory.04.9.title": "Counting for a task",
  "grammar.audit.theory.04.11": "A: いついきますか。 — When are you going?<br>B: ごがつふつかにいきます。 — I am going on May 2.<br>A: みっかはどうですか。 — How about the 3rd?<br>Learn the date within an appointment: ふつか (day 2), みっか (day 3). The exercise and practice use this distinction again.",
  "grammar.audit.theory.04.11.title": "Dates for a plan",
  "grammar.audit.theory.05.8": "A: どうしておくれましたか。 — Why were you late?<br>B: でんしゃがおそかったんです。 — The train was late, you see.<br>んです provides the explanation connecting to the question. It does not add a new cause by itself. おくれる = be late; でんしゃ = train; おそい = late/slow.",
  "grammar.audit.theory.05.8.title": "An explanation in dialogue",
  "grammar.audit.theory.07.5": "<span class=\"grammar-contrast\"><span>くすりをのまなくてはいけません<small>obligation: I have to take the medicine</small></span><span>ここでたべてはいけません<small>prohibition: you cannot eat here</small></span><span>やすんだほうがいいです<small>advice: it would be better to rest</small></span></span>Read the form before the ending: なくて / て / た change the intention. くすり = medicine; やすむ = rest.",
  "grammar.audit.theory.07.5.title": "Obligation, prohibition and advice",
  "grammar.audit.10.9.idea": "In practice, the error summary identifies concepts you missed. Reviewing errors creates a round with only those activities; return to theory if you do not understand why.",
  "grammar.audit.09.10.caption": "I give to someone else.",
  "grammar.audit.09.11.caption": "Someone else gives to me.",
  "grammar.audit.09.12.caption": "I receive from someone else.",
